hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1719","Narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim and Yahya ibn Hakim, who said: Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, and Yahya said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, saying: Hind bint al-Harith narrated to me, from Umm Salamah (RA), that:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he would finish the prayer with the taslim"," would not remain seated except for a short while"," until the women would leave.\""\n\nAl-Zuhri said: \""And Allah knows best"," this was so that the women could leave before any of the men would exit.\""\n\nYahya ibn Hakim said: \""He would not remain seated except for a short while.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
